after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material public-task outcomes are satisfied. The provider restart protocol is also strong: it captures a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, connection loss, a changed boot identity, and recovery of the running service with its identity and resource limits intact. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["The CPU sample calculated 25.18% using a nominal four-second denominator, slightly above the label value; its approximately 4.096-second command duration, exact kernel quota, and throttling in every observed period indicate measurement-window imprecision rather than a demonstrated limit breach (cmd-d9eecd0abf164d4e).","Memory enforcement was directly established through the kernel memory.max value, but no workload was driven to the 128 MiB boundary to observe an allocation failure or OOM event.","The restart evidence has no separate application-data or multi-node cluster-state probe; the supplied environment contains a single stateless worker, so recovery evidence covers node and service state."]}
